  "reason": "The current best (config_039, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted. All top results confirm multiprofile+transformer is strong, but the singleprofile architecture with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l remains completely untested. Config_007 (singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted) isolates the single most important unexplored architectural dimension—whether multiprofile+transformer aggregation is truly necessary or whether a simpler single-profile path with the same strong encoders could match or exceed 0.725. This resolves high uncertainty with the best-known component choices. If it underperforms, it confirms the multiprofile+transformer design and lets the final 2 experiments focus on fine-tuning within that space; if it performs comparably or better, it opens a new promising direction. With only 2 experiments remaining, reducing this architectural uncertainty is the highest-value use of the next slot."
